## Objective: Retrieve the Golden Peach

The Golden Peach is hidden somewhere on the estate grounds. It is not in any of the six main areas. It is in a seventh location — the Crescent Alcove — a narrow passage between Areas 3 and 6 that does not appear on any obvious path. It can only be identified from the Obelisk, and only if a player looks specifically at the spaces between areas rather than the areas themselves.

**Floor Clear Condition:** Return the Golden Peach to the starting hexagonal courtyard.

---

## The Center — The Hexagonal Courtyard

> *The floor opens onto a wide stone courtyard, hexagonal in shape, paved in pale grey with silver veins running through the rock. Six paths branch outward from it, evenly spaced, each one leading into a different part of the estate. The architecture here is clean, almost severe — white walls, arched doorways, lanterns burning with cold blue flame.*
>
> *In the very center of the courtyard stands an obelisk of pale stone, perhaps fifteen feet tall. Near its top, at each face, is a narrow arched window. A spiral staircase winds around the outside.*
>
> *The courtyard itself is empty. No guards patrol here. It is, for now, a safe zone.*

**The Obelisk:**
- Climbing and using it takes **10 minutes**
- From the windows, a player can observe any one area at a time — they must specify which direction they are looking
- **What it reveals:** The visual character of the area — its obstacle type, guard composition, and the general nature of the check required (see each area's Obelisk entry below)
- **Information goes stale after 30 minutes** — guard positions shift with the trap cycle, and scouted intel from before the last cycle may no longer be accurate
- **One at a time** — the staircase is narrow; a second player cannot use it while another is up there
- **Spotting the Alcove:** If a player specifically asks to look at the space *between* areas rather than the areas themselves, and they are looking between Areas 3 and 6, they may make a **DC 14 Perception check**. On a success, they notice a faint golden shimmer in a narrow gap in the wall — not an area, but a passage. This is the Crescent Alcove.

