## Alert System

Each area has its own alert level, tracked independently. A fight in Area 2 does not automatically affect Area 5, but it may affect adjacent areas depending on how loud it gets.

| Level | State | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | Normal | Standard patrol, standard Passive Perception |
| 1 | Alerted | Guards move faster; Passive Perception +2; will investigate unusual sounds |
| 2 | Searching | Guards actively sweep; Stealth DCs increase by 4; Warden joins patrol if not already present |

**Alert drops one level every 15 minutes if nothing further happens.**

**Noise from combat or a failed check in one area raises the alert level of adjacent areas by 1 step.** Players should be aware that a messy Area 2 run will make Area 3 harder for whoever goes next — including the other party if two groups are operating simultaneously.

---

## The 30-Minute Trap Cycle

The estate has a rhythm. Three events rotate in sequence. Players who survive long enough will notice the pattern.

**DM Note:** Track elapsed time from the moment the floor is entered. Trigger events at the listed intervals. If two parties enter at different times, track their personal timers separately — but the environmental events affect the floor as a whole. Both parties feel the same Moonfall even if they entered at different times.

---

### Cycle A — Moonfall *(First trigger: minute 30, then every 90 minutes)*

> *A low resonance passes through the floor. Then, for three minutes, fine silver shards rain down across two randomly chosen areas — not the center.*

Roll 2d6 (1–6 = Area 1–6, reroll duplicates) to determine affected areas. For the duration:
- Any player in an affected area attempting a check must make a **DC 12 Constitution save** or take 1d4 piercing damage and have their check time **doubled** as they shield themselves
- Guards in affected areas become **Alerted** (step 1) regardless of prior status

---

### Cycle B — Patrol Surge *(First trigger: minute 60, then every 90 minutes)*

> *Somewhere in the estate, a horn sounds — short, sharp, professional. Footsteps multiply.*

Each area gains **one additional Scout Rabbit** for 20 minutes. After 20 minutes, the Scouts return to barracks and guard compositions return to normal. Areas that were already Alerted remain Alerted.

---

### Cycle C — Silver Fog *(First trigger: minute 90, then every 90 minutes)*

> *A low silver mist rolls in from the edges of the courtyard. It doesn't obscure vision badly, but it thickens the air around the obelisk.*

For 10 minutes, the obelisk takes **15 minutes to use** instead of 10. Passive Perception in the center courtyard drops by 2 (the fog muffles sound and softens edges). Guards do not enter the center, so this primarily affects player scouting decisions.

