## Check Resolution

Each area requires a character to succeed on a check to make progress. **Only one character may perform the primary check at a time.** Others may assist (granting advantage) if it logically makes sense, but the assist character is also present and exposed to guard detection.

**Time required per check:** Roll 1d6 at the start of the attempt.

| Roll | Time Required |
|---|---|
| 1–2 | 5 minutes |
| 3–4 | 8 minutes |
| 5 | 12 minutes |
| 6 | 15 minutes |

A **Natural 1** on the check doubles the time before failure is confirmed — and then the character must fight or flee.
A **Natural 20** halves the time required (round down, minimum 1 minute).

**On Failure:** The character must fight or flee back to the center. If they flee, area alert level raises by 1. If they fight and win, the area can be reattempted — but at Alert level 1.

